      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You can frame this tension as a shift from short-term profit maximization to long-term value creation. Traditional shareholder primacy prioritizes immediate financial returns, while ESG integrates environmental and social factors into decision-making. Explain that strong ESG performance mitigates risks—like regulatory fines or supply chain disruptions—which ultimately protects and enhances long-term profitability. This approach moves the discussion from \"cost\" to \"risk management\" and \"future resilience.\"",
